    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive profile, anchored by **Junior Caminero** (84.24), who stands as our premier start despite a 36% rain risk. His matchup against Young provides a significant boost, buoyed by a +16% park factor and a +12% SP skill advantage. Joining him at the top of the projected efficiency ratings are **Trea Turner** (79.76) and **Kyle Schwarber** (78.41). Both benefit immensely from the matchup against Mathews, as the +19% SP skill advantage aligns with favorable wind conditions and aggressive top-of-the-order usage, making them essential pivots for Roto production. **Yordan Alvarez** (74.02) also remains a must-start; while the platoon disadvantage against left-hander Lopez slightly caps his ceiling, his elite xwOBA of 0.460 overrides the marginal negative platoon splits.\n\nWe are leveraging significant platoon and situational edges today, specifically with **Lars Nootbaar** (67.76) and **Caleb Durbin** (66.08). **Nootbaar** earns a massive +11% boost from a favorable platoon matchup against Lowder, while **Durbin** capitalizes on a +14% SP skill advantage in a hitter-friendly environment. Our most difficult decision on the bench was **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (54.04). He flirted with a starting spot due to his leadoff placement (+10% order bonus), but ultimately fell short of **Christian Yelich** and **Carson Benge** due to a projected -15% dynamic platoon hit against Anderson, forcing us to bench him to preserve game caps and prioritize higher raw efficiency.\n\nRisk management remains a primary focus, particularly regarding the weather. Both **Junior Caminero** and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (66.65) are tied to a 36% rain probability in their respective contests; we will monitor the situation closely, though their high projected scores currently justify the risk. **Dillon Dingler** (46.16) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (51.51) represent our lower-tier starters today. **Dillon Dingler** specifically suffers from a -15% platoon penalty against Wacha, and while he remains in the lineup to maintain our counting stats, he is on the low end of our efficiency threshold. We remain ready to pivot to bench assets like **Hector Rodriguez** or **Chase Meidroth** should the weather reports for the early afternoon games deteriorate.",
